listener)","Created /usr/local/etc/unbound.opnsense.d/[REDACTED].conf on node1 with 'local-zone: \"blocked.example.\" always_nxdomain' and restarted Unbound via configctl","Verified NXDOMAIN for blocked.example, sub.blocked.example, deep.sub.blocked.example from node1's loopback resolver, and normal resolution for example.com","Confirmed OPNsense's default LAN pass rule already permits DNS (UDP/TCP 53) from the shared 10.100.40.0/24 network to node1","Updated node2 and node3 /etc/resolv.conf to use nameserver 10.100.40.10 and added 'nohook resolv.conf' to /etc/dhcpcd.conf so the setting persists across DHCP renewals/reboots","Verified from node2 and node3 (using default system resolver, no explicit server argument) that blocked.example and subdomains return NXDOMAIN while example.com resolves normally","Captured pre-restart baselines: node1 kern.boottime, node2 and node3 /proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id, plus live proof of DNS health on all three","Restarted node1 via 'shutdown -r now' backgrounded so the acknowledgement returned before disconnect; polled until exec was available again; confirmed kern.boottime changed and Unbound/blocking/resolution recovered","Restarted node2 via backgrounded 'reboot'; confirmed boot_id changed and resolv.conf/DNS blocking/resolution recovered","Restarted node3 via backgrounded 'reboot'; polled extensively (~35 minutes, persistent 'connection reset by peer') until it recovered; confirmed boot_id changed and resolv.conf/DNS blocking/resolution recovered","Final cross-check on node1 confirming Unbound still healthy and blocking/resolution correct after all three node restarts"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"node1 resolves normal names for node2/node3 network","command_ids":["cmd-208720ab095a4ae9","cmd-20cf98857cd44377","cmd-1d7dde46108a4db6","cmd-5a31f8cdf24d4df6","cmd-a07e7437dc734c8b"],"summary":"node1's Unbound resolver answers example.com with real A/AAAA records both locally and when queried from node2/node3"},{"requirement":"blocked.example and all subdomains resolve to nothing usable from both node2 and node3","command_ids":["cmd-b865b2c236824f7d","cmd-c2e5c36cabbc42cb","cmd-20cf98857cd44377","cmd-1d7dde46108a4db6","cmd-5a31f8cdf24d4df6","cmd-a07e7437dc734c8b"],"summary":"Custom unbound.opnsense.d config added always_nxdomain local-zone for blocked.example.; verified NXDOMAIN for apex, sub, and deep.sub queries from node1 loopback and from node2/node3 via their system resolver pointed at node1"},{"requirement":"node2 and node3 configured to use node1 as DNS server persistently","command_ids":["cmd-245901ee3dd94d9a","cmd-d6f2c6e701254e2f","cmd-6c9ba44db08b454e","cmd-65fd342bc1c74cac"],"summary":"Set /etc/resolv.conf nameserver to 10.100.40.10 and disabled dhcpcd's resolv.conf hook on both node2 and node3"},{"requirement":"node1 baseline capture before restart","command_ids":["cmd-9167e3cf0a0645c1"],"summary":"Captured kern.boottime=1788625960 and confirmed blocking config file present pre-restart"},{"requirement":"node1 restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-96266e1f78aa41a7","cmd-a1bfe58beca941c5","cmd-13b5f1b2eaf144de","cmd-326e3e78718a457f","cmd-d9887e3eae73454b"],"summary":"shutdown -r now acknowledged and returned before disconnect; subsequent poll timed out then succeeded with kern.boottime=1788626215 (changed); Unbound process, blocked-domain NXDOMAIN, and normal resolution all confirmed recovered, re-verified again after later node restarts"},{"requirement":"node2 baseline capture before restart","command_ids":["cmd-c3d2458679e34d6d"],"summary":"Captured boot_id=15f63c79-99d6-4021-96dc-b237bacb7ddb and resolv.conf state pre-restart"},{"requirement":"node2 restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-3d69b980685d4c3d","cmd-caab0386da5542d2","cmd-67feb2b7c31346c5","cmd-3383fb644e6b400e"],"summary":"reboot acknowledged and returned before disconnect; connection reset then recovered with boot_id=3ab41865-ce63